{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154674-help-groking-the-umbra","id":1154674,"title":"Help groking the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-01T05:43:44-07:00","id":1154674,"title":"Help groking the Umbra","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Hi everyone, I am a new ST with a bunch of new players playing Werewolf. One of th things I am having more trouble is understanding how to use the Umbra, I get that it is supposed to be up to the DM what it looks like and how it behaves and for what I have seen in the discussions on this forum opinions varies wildly. The thing is I don't have a starting point to start developing form, I find the book of the Umbra too esoteric (Duh).</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">As for the specific questions</span></span></span></span><br /> <ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">If a Garou dies in the Umbra, do they dissolve and go into slumber or the corpse just stays there for scavenging spirits to eat?</span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The penumbra in the wilderness is described as pure explosion of life and trees and smells, are all trees in the penumbra slumbered spirits waiting to be awakened or are they just &quot;props&quot;?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">How many spirits are typically in the penumbra? Again I get that that is a choice of the ST depending on how it fits the story but some guidelines would be nice, are they expected to be able to track and find a couple of animal spirits in a penumbra forest?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Is the river they find in the penumbra a river spirit or do they need to invoke it if they want to talk with it as with other spirits?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Does it make sense to find a cold or snow spirit during a blizzard in the material world? </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Is reasonable of a town to have the spirit of a dog, a reflection of all the hunting</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> and guardian dogs that have lived in the town for generations? </span></span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Do banes that stick to a person for possession or feeding follow that person through the umbra floating where that person is?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Are all banes aggressive by nature and will attack the Garous?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">If despair falls into a town does a bane representing that despair appear from that despair or arrives called by it?</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I hope this is not too much and thank you in advance for helping me with any of this stuff.</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","name":"Hares666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T07:54:40-07:00","id":1154710,"title":"","content":"Hey, welcome to the World of Darkness and Werewolf in particular<br /> <br /> If a garou dies in the Umbra then it's body remains unless they are in a realm where otherwise would occur.<br /> <br /> The WTA cosmology is a Gnostic reality meaning that yes, everything will have a spirit. Now when you have things in the Penumbra that are the echoes of things past (for example trees where there is now a parking lot) those will still be spirits in slumber but that slumber will be VERY deep and the spirits if awoken will be very weak and quickly return to their slumber.<br /> <br /> In a city you will see the Weaver and the Wyrm represented all over. In the depths of the wilderness you'll find Naturae with more regularity. Again much of these will not be than the most rudimentary gafflings and ultimately population levels should come down to requirement. <br /> <br /> In regards to the river the answer is 'yes' to both. The River itself will be the penumbral reflection but it will have a Spirit of Itself too the form of which varies on how powerful that spirit is. A gaffling river spirit for example will pretty much just be the river, a jaggling of greater power though may appear as a washer woman on it's banks or a swarming shoal of fish or rippling eddies or the voice of the river birds that swim and feed there etc<br /> <br /> Yes, it makes total sense<br /> <br /> Again, if it's something you want or need in the game yes, it makes perfect sense as that would be an Engling as opposed to a Naturae of a dog<br /> <br /> In the case of possess the bane occupies the person (but might be detectable within the umbral shadow) banes that are feeding from/encouraging action of a person will indeed be flocking near that person, or be near by.<br /> <br /> All Banes tend to be aggressive to a degree but like all spirits their exact nature depends on exactly WHAT they are and how powerful a Bane they are. They will not necessarily attack the Garou but they will be hostile (even if they are fleeing) it's also worth noting that banes tend to be more active enmasse during the day. <br /> <br /> To the last one it's a bit of both, despair will attract banes of that nature and could also easily birth more of the same or similar. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:34:32-07:00","id":1154785,"title":"","content":"I had many of the same questions as you when I began to ST. Below are my answers which is a combination of printed material, and my own extrapolations and interpretations.<br /> <br /> If a Garou dies, their body remains in the umbra. Eventually the body will dissolve/convert into pure ephemera and disappear.<br /> <br /> The penumbra will almost always show a fairly accurate representation of the natural world in terms of geographic features, rock, and plants. Very few of these things are spiritually active though unless they are a living creature, extremely old, and were importantly appreciated by people near them for generations. However, otherwise they still have spirits, they are just in slumber and can be awakened. Artificial constructs created by Man only appear in the umbra tentatively, lack detail, and are less real - unless spirits of the Weaver like Pattern Spiders &quot;reinforce&quot; it OR that object has special significance for the people living there over time. There really are not &quot;props&quot; in the Penumbra, but they can appear in Near Realms. &quot;Props&quot; would be what the game calls Emanations - they are made of ephemera, but are not spirits. Instead Emanations are kind of like puppets created and controlled by the Realm itself in order to create a specific experience for any visitors who arrive there (the people and some of the animals in Wolfhome for example, are all Emanations).<br /> <br /> The game has been inconsistent in its editions and supplements on how many spirits exist. My guidelines is that it really depends on the spiritual power in each part of the world. Where you have caerns and domains (Glens, Blights, Webs, etc.) you have lots of spirits. In a Caern or Glen, Gaia spirits probably equal to the regular animal population. But those are relatively rare though. As you get farther away from them, the spirit population drops correspondingly. In areas far from any Domains (such as suburbs which are not strongly resonant enough to attract Glens, Webs, or Hellholes), it is kind of a spiritual wasteland with only scattered individual spirits able to be found. In a place like the city that is dominated by Webs and a few Blights and perhaps a few Hellholes, most spirits will be Weaver and then Wyrm. Only the biggest parks in the city may shelter a small Glen which is the only source of Gaian nature spirits. That park will be a beacon for local Garou to try and protect, and only a few small Gaian spirits will wander outside the park to explore, and they'll be preyed upon by the other kind of spirits. My advice to you is to have a general map of the area in your head (are on a piece of paper) and plant where you want the various Domains to be and how large/powerful they are. That will be your guide to the normal spirit population.<br /> <br /> Whether things like already have an awakened spirit attached to it depends on its spiritual significance and ideas that people have. Usually bodies of water are things that have spirits because rivers, ponds, and lakes are given distinctive names and even assigned personalities. Certainly any large sized river or bodies of water probably have a Jaggling spirit although small creeks and such may not. In which case, the water of the river will exist as ephemeral water, and somewhere around it will be the spirit of that river as well.<br /> <br /> Yes. In fact any time the weather changes, I almost always have appropriate spirits show up to &quot;create&quot; that in the Realm. When thunderstorms happen, those spirits (storm spirits, thunder spirits, rain spirits, etc.) ,show up in the Penumbra to make it happen. When snow falls, it's because snow and ice spirits show up. When the wind kicks up, wind spirits blow by. If there is a bad blizzard out in the wilderness that really buries the plants under snow and makes hunting difficult, you might even see a Wendigo in that blizzard.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can have a dog spirit in town. Domesticated animals have spirits too. The game didn't give us a name for any kind of Domain for them, but in my games I do have such domains connected to Wolfhome. These are for spirits that have accepted Man as their Master. Such domains, for want of a better word we can call them Pastorals for now, probably exist in idyllic farming communities and very small towns. And certainly dog spirits and cat spirits can spread from there to suburbs and cities. Such spirits, certainly for pets, may also just spontaneously appear because of the love and comradeship people have for their pets.<br /> <br /> If a bane possesses the person, they are now part of that person or occupying their space. If a bane is feeding on the person, then they'd be around the person. Note that people usually are not seen in the umbra - they are not spiritually advanced/aware to show up there. Only people who are spiritually advanced, for good or evil, would show up to a certain degree in the umbra itself. In my games, people who have True Faith, Hedge Magic, Numina, and similar abilities show up. So would great spiritual leaders who may not have supernatural powers. So do people who are able to contact the Periphery of the Umbra. However, many of these people may not show up as distinct people with recognizable features, but more of a generic, vague outline. If someone gets possessed by a Bane, I would say they definitely appear in the umbra in some way. How distinctive is up to you based on how easy you want Garou to notice these kind of things. And you can always rule that certain mundane Banes clearly show up, but that special Banes have some kind of mask or other concealment that prevent that from happening.<br /> <br /> Generally it depends on the kind of spirit. Gafflings, even those that can talk and communicate, are really no more intelligent than animals. If it is in their nature to attack on site, then they will. Jagglings though are at least as intelligent as humans, and they will consider things first. Maybe it is stupid to attack the Garou on site, or the spirit has some cunning plan, so they won't. And because Jagglings control any Gafflings they spin off from themselves, THEIR gafflings will obey their commands.<br /> <br /> Yes, mass despair in a town could attract a Bane that feeds on it and causes even more misery. Whether or not it does or not, or if it becomes any kind of problem in the Realm, always depends if you want to use it for plot purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:59:33-07:00","id":1154792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154674-help-groking-the-umbra?p=1154710#post1154710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WTA cosmology is a Gnostic reality meaning that yes, everything will have a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Annoying pedantry] An Animist reality is one where everything, including plants, inanimate objects and natural phenomenon have a soul/spirit. A Gnostic reality is one based on esoteric mystical knowledge known only to an elect few. Generally speaking, Werewolf is a Dark Animist cosmology, while Mage is a Dark Gnostic one. [/annoying pedantry] <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it makes total sense </div> </div> </div>It does, yes. It just sometimes requires being able to keep two potentially contradictory or at least irrational concept in your head at the same time, with &quot;As a Garou, I'm both a being of flesh and a powerful spirit at the same time&quot; being just one of the smaller ones. Wolf-born Garou seem to have an easier time accepting this, probably because they don't have to unlearn the human way of looking at the world. IIRC, this is part of why they have such high starting Gnosis scores. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:34:54-07:00","id":1154804,"title":"","content":"I'm here just to add a few things, most of the answers are good already as they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hares666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1154674-help-groking-the-umbra#post1154674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it make sense to find a cold or snow spirit during a blizzard in the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! They're going to be around anyway when the weather is cold enough (aka winter).<br /> But also remember that the weather in the Umbra is related to the emotional state of the inhabitant in the material world; so a peaceful village with people chilling at the fireside during a hailstorm is still going to have a pleasant weather beyond the Gauntlet while a hurricane could cause an Umbral hurricane if it stirs enough panic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do banes that stick to a person for possession or feeding follow that person through the umbra floating where that person is? </div> </div> </div>If they're feeding they're going to be somewhere around the person in the Umbra. You won't see the person though.<br /> There is no clear RAW about fomori umbral reflection, but I assume they still have none: the Bane is bound into the fomori, so it only exists in the material world (just as fetishes or materialized spirits). Of course, if the Fomori goes in the Umbra than the bane is going to be in the Umbra too, they're merged. =p<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are all banes aggressive by nature and will attack the Garous? </div> </div> </div>No, there was a manual (can't remember which one, maybe Velvet Shadow) saying that banes won't attack a Garou approaching them peacefully and that they'll be usually looking for a way to corrupt them, offering some kind of Faustian deal. A good werewolf usually won't bargain with them, though. =P Some banes are going to make more sense in this kind of role, of course: banes of violence or fury aren't just as talkative as a blood money one, gafflings may be too stupid to conversate (even if they could call their jaggling master, though), while bane elementals have the same single-mindedness of the regular elementals and won't probably attack unless you mess with their polluting agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-02-2017, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T00:50:58-07:00","id":1154996,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone, all your answers have help me a great deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20067-hares666","name":"Hares666","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}